<title>USA: nStor sees 1997 EPS of $0.20 or more.</title>
<headline>nStor sees 1997 EPS of $0.20 or more.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>nStor Technologies  Inc on Tuesday said that it expected 1997 earnings of at least $0.20 per share and sales of about $45 million.</p>
<p>The company, which makes UNIX-based memory products and digital media-management products, issued the statement at its annual shareholders meeting in New York.</p>
<p>The company is headquartered in West Palm Beach, Florida, and its primary operating subsidiary, nStor Corp Inc, is based in Lake Mary, Florida.</p>
